#: shortcuts.cpp:98
msgid ""
"<h1>Key Bindings</h1> Using key bindings you can configure certain actions "
"to be triggered when you press a key or a combination of keys, e.g. Ctrl+C "
"is normally bound to 'Copy'. KDE allows you to store more than one 'scheme' "
"of key bindings, so you might want to experiment a little setting up your "
"own scheme while you can still change back to the KDE defaults."
"<p>"
" In the tab 'Global Shortcuts' you can configure non-application specific "
"bindings like how to switch desktops or maximize a window. In the tab "
"'Application Shortcuts' you will find bindings typically used in "
"applications, such as copy and paste."
msgstr ""

